@page "/multivariate"

<PageTitle>Combo Stability Calculator - Card Game Calculator</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">Combo Stability Calculator</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-6" Color="Color.Secondary">
    Calculate the probability of drawing the required pieces of a multi-part combination.
    Uses the multivariate hypergeometric distribution — all groups draw from the same deck,
    so their probabilities are not independent.
</MudText>

<MudExpansionPanels Class="mb-6" MultiExpansion="true">
    <MudExpansionPanel Text="Theory & Math">
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            The <strong>multivariate hypergeometric distribution</strong> extends the single-group model
            to \(G\) distinct card groups drawn simultaneously from the same deck. All groups compete for
            the same \(n\) draws, so their probabilities are <em>correlated</em> — drawing more of one
            group leaves fewer slots for the others.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-1">Probability of drawing exactly \(k_i\) from each group</MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ P(X_1 = k_1, \ldots, X_G = k_G) = \frac{\displaystyle\prod_{i=1}^{G}\binom{K_i}{k_i} \cdot \binom{N - \sum_{i=1}^{G} K_i}{\;n - \sum_{i=1}^{G} k_i\;}}{\binom{N}{n}} $$
        </div>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            The term \(\binom{N - \sum K_i}{n - \sum k_i}\) counts the ways to fill the remaining draw
            slots from cards that belong to <em>no</em> defined group.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-1">Probability that every group meets its minimum simultaneously</MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ P(X_1 \geq m_1, \ldots, X_G \geq m_G) = \frac{1}{\binom{N}{n}} \!\! \sum_{\substack{k_i \geq m_i \\ k_1 + \cdots + k_G \leq n}} \prod_{i=1}^{G}\binom{K_i}{k_i} \cdot \binom{N - \sum K_i}{n - \sum k_i} $$
        </div>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            This sums all valid draw tuples \((k_1, \ldots, k_G)\) where each group meets its minimum and
            the total does not exceed \(n\). The enumeration is performed recursively group by group,
            which keeps computation tractable for typical combo sizes.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mt-2 mb-2">Parameters</MudText>
        <MudText>\(N\) — deck size</MudText>
        <MudText>\(K_i\) — number of cards in group \(i\)</MudText>
        <MudText>\(m_i\) — minimum copies required from group \(i\)</MudText>
        <MudText>\(n\) — cards drawn (hand size)</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">\(G\) — number of groups</MudText>

        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" Dense="true">
            You <strong>cannot</strong> multiply individual group probabilities together to get the joint
            probability. All groups draw from the same deck, creating a negative correlation — assembling
            one combo piece slightly reduces the chances of finding another.
        </MudAlert>
    </MudExpansionPanel>

    <MudExpansionPanel Text="How to Use">
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            Define the deck parameters and each card group, then press <strong>Calculate</strong>.
            The probability curve shows how the assembly chance grows with additional draws. Use
            the Monte Carlo simulation to empirically verify the closed-form result.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-2">Example — Three-Piece Combo in Standard</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-2">
            Your 60-card deck needs three combo pieces to win. You run 4 copies of each.
            What is the probability of holding all three in your opening hand of 7?
        </MudText>
        <ol style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <li>Deck Size: <strong>60</strong>, Cards Drawn: <strong>7</strong></li>
            <li>Group 1 — "Piece A": In Deck <strong>4</strong>, Want <strong>1</strong></li>
            <li>Group 2 — "Piece B": In Deck <strong>4</strong>, Want <strong>1</strong></li>
            <li>Group 3 — "Piece C": In Deck <strong>4</strong>, Want <strong>1</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            Press <strong>Calculate</strong>. The <em>At least minimum of each group</em> result is the
            probability of opening with the full combo — approximately <strong>1.57%</strong>. The curve
            shows how quickly this improves as you draw more cards.
        </MudText>

        <MudDivider Class="my-4" />

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-2">Example — Reanimator Deck in Standard</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-2">
            Your 100-card singleton reanimator deck needs three roles covered in hand: a Reanimation Target
            (10 copies), a Reanimation Spell (12 copies), and a Self-mill Card (20 copies).
            What is the probability of having at least one of each in your opening hand of 7?
        </MudText>
        <ol style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <li>Deck Size: <strong>100</strong>, Cards Drawn: <strong>7</strong></li>
            <li>Group 1 — "Reanimation Targets": In Deck <strong>10</strong>, Want <strong>1</strong></li>
            <li>Group 2 — "Reanimation Spells": In Deck <strong>12</strong>, Want <strong>1</strong></li>
            <li>Group 3 — "Self-mill Cards": In Deck <strong>20</strong>, Want <strong>1</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <MudText>
            Press <strong>Calculate</strong>. Because this deck runs far more copies of each role than the
            strict 4-copy example above, the opening-hand probability is significantly higher — demonstrating
            the value of redundancy in combo decks.
        </MudText>
    </MudExpansionPanel>
</MudExpansionPanels>

<MudGrid>
    <MudItem xs="12" md="4">
        <MudCard Elevation="2">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Parameters</MudText>
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                <MudGrid Spacing="2" Class="mb-5">
                    <MudItem xs="6">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_deckSize" Label="Deck Size" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                            Min="1" Max="999" HelperText="Total cards (N)" />
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="6">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_drawCount" Label="Cards Drawn" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                            Min="1" Max="@_deckSize" HelperText="Hand size (n)" />
                    </MudItem>
                </MudGrid>

                <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-2">Card Groups</MudText>

                @foreach (var group in _groups)
                {
                    <MudGrid Spacing="1" Class="mb-1">
                        <MudItem xs="5">
                            <MudTextField @bind-Value="group.Name" Label="Name"
                                Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" />
                        </MudItem>
                        <MudItem xs="3">
                            <MudNumericField @bind-Value="group.CopiesInDeck" Label="In Deck"
                                Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" Min="0" Max="@_deckSize" />
                        </MudItem>
                        <MudItem xs="3">
                            <MudNumericField @bind-Value="group.DesiredCopies" Label="Want"
                                Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" Min="0" Max="@group.CopiesInDeck" />
                        </MudItem>
                        <MudItem xs="1" Class="d-flex align-center justify-center">
                            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Delete" Color="Color.Error"
                                Size="Size.Small" OnClick="@(() => RemoveGroup(group))" />
                        </MudItem>
                    </MudGrid>
                }

                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Color="Color.Primary" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add"
                    OnClick="AddGroup" Class="mt-2">
                    Add Group
                </MudButton>

                @if (_validationError is not null)
                {
                    <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning" Class="mt-3" Dense="true">@_validationError</MudAlert>
                }
            </MudCardContent>
            <MudCardActions Class="flex-column px-4 pb-4 pt-0">
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" OnClick="Calculate" FullWidth="true"
                    StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Calculate" Class="mb-2">
                    Calculate
                </MudButton>
                <MudTooltip Text="Resets Deck Size and Cards Drawn to the defaults of the currently selected format. Clears the current results.">
                    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="ResetToFormat" FullWidth="true"
                        StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.RestartAlt">
                        Reset to chosen format
                    </MudButton>
                </MudTooltip>
            </MudCardActions>
        </MudCard>

        @if (_calculated)
        {
            <MudCard Elevation="2" Class="mt-4">
                <MudCardHeader>
                    <CardHeaderContent>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Results — @_drawCount cards drawn</MudText>
                    </CardHeaderContent>
                </MudCardHeader>
                <MudCardContent Class="pa-0">
                    <MudList T="string" Dense="true">
                        <MudListItem>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary">At least minimum of each group</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" Color="Color.Primary">@_atLeastProb.ToString("P2")</MudText>
                        </MudListItem>
                        <MudDivider />
                        <MudListItem>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary">Exactly the desired of each group</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" Color="Color.Primary">@_exactProb.ToString("P2")</MudText>
                        </MudListItem>
                    </MudList>
                </MudCardContent>
            </MudCard>
        }
    </MudItem>

    <MudItem xs="12" md="8">
        <MudCard Elevation="2">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Probability vs Cards Drawn</MudText>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">
                        Chance of drawing at least the minimum from every group simultaneously
                    </MudText>
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                @if (_calculated)
                {
                    <PlotlyChart Config="_chartConfig" Layout="_chartLayout" Data="_chartData" @ref="_chart" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <MudPaper Class="d-flex align-center justify-center" Style="height:350px;" Elevation="0">
                        <MudText Color="Color.Secondary">Press Calculate to see the probability curve.</MudText>
                    </MudPaper>
                }
            </MudCardContent>
        </MudCard>

        <MudCard Elevation="2" Class="mt-4">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Simulation</MudText>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">
                        Empirical verification via Monte Carlo sampling
                    </MudText>
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                <MudGrid Spacing="2" Class="mb-2" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center">
                    <MudItem xs="7">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_simulationIterations" Label="Iterations"
                            Variant="Variant.Outlined" Min="1000" Max="1000000" Step="10000" />
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="5">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_confidenceLevel" Label="Confidence %"
                            Variant="Variant.Outlined" Min="50" Max="99" />
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="12" Class="d-flex flex-column">
                        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Secondary" OnClick="RunSimulation"
                            StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.PlayArrow"
                            Disabled="!_calculated || _simulationRunning">
                            Run
                        </MudButton>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mt-2"
                            Style="@(_simulationRunning ? "visibility: visible;" : "visibility: hidden;")">
                            Simulating&hellip;
                        </MudText>
                    </MudItem>
                </MudGrid>

                @if (_simulationResult is not null)
                {
                    double delta = _simulationResult.Probability - _atLeastProb;
                    string deltaSign = delta >= 0 ? "+" : "";

                    <MudGrid Spacing="2" Class="mt-2">
                        <MudItem xs="12" sm="4">
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary">Empirical Probability</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5">@_simulationResult.Probability.ToString("P2")</MudText>
                        </MudItem>
                        <MudItem xs="12" sm="5">
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary">@(_simulationResult.ConfidenceLevel.ToString("P0")) Confidence Interval</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                                @_simulationResult.ConfidenceIntervalLow.ToString("P2") — @_simulationResult.ConfidenceIntervalHigh.ToString("P2")
                            </MudText>
                        </MudItem>
                        <MudItem xs="12" sm="3">
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary">Delta vs Analytical</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.body1"
                                Color="@(Math.Abs(delta) < 0.005 ? Color.Success : Color.Warning)">
                                @($"{deltaSign}{delta:P2}")
                            </MudText>
                        </MudItem>
                    </MudGrid>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mt-1">
                        @_simulationResult.Successes.ToString("N0") successes in @_simulationResult.Iterations.ToString("N0") iterations
                    </MudText>
                }
                else
                {
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">
                        @(_calculated ? "Ready to run." : "Run the analytical calculation first.")
                    </MudText>
                }
            </MudCardContent>
        </MudCard>
    </MudItem>
</MudGrid>
